From edfbc2ebe833ccfa242442cf21e8c33a3777be43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DanTyldesley <dan@DanTyldesleys-MacBook-Air.local>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 12:48:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Messaging: chat human-handoff toggle + Messaging agent-setup
 subpage

Adds a chat-specific human-handoff switch, independent of the voice-side
humanEscalation, so a garage can allow phone transfers while keeping chat
fully AI-handled (or vice versa).

- schema: messagingHumanHandoff (default true) + messagingHandoffMessage
- config route: exposes + persists both fields (get + save)
- chatAgentAssist/V2/Tyresoft: read messagingHumanHandoff for chat; when off,
  strip take-message/callback tools and use messagingHandoffMessage verbatim
  (falls back to phone/email contact if blank)
- new Agent Setup > Messaging subpage (MessagingTab) gated by hasMessagingAccess
  via the per-garage messaging-access endpoint; staff always see it
- Sidebar flyout: threads hasMessagingAccess into AgentConfigSidebarItem so the
  gated nav item resolves correctly

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
